# Erenimbus hunter, SysID 1: simulation interface parameters.
# Load after gazebo-plane.parm. This configuration isolates aircraft-model
# effects when comparing visual guidance. Airframe-specific servo mapping,
# autotune gains, TECS tuning, AHRS_TRIM_Y, takeoff and steering parameters
# remain those of the reference gazebo-plane configuration.
#
# Hunter SysID is 1 and target SysID is 2. ArduPlane 4.7 names this parameter
# MAV_SYSID. The former SYSID_THISMAV name is rejected by this build.
MAV_SYSID 1

# Enable synthetic airspeed for speed-command response. This setup has no
# pitot sensor. Its Gazebo backend reports zero fdm.airspeed because it does
# not call Aircraft::update_dynamics(). With TECS_SYNAIRSPEED = 0, AP_TECS
# selects _update_throttle_without_airspeed() and _SKE_weighting = 0.
# Commands 178 and 43000 may then return ACCEPTED without changing speed.
# The same effect is documented in params/target.parm.
TECS_SYNAIRSPEED 1

# Bound synthetic airspeed error. Without a sensor:
# IAS = |V_gps(NED) - W_EKF3| / EAS2TAS.
# With drag fusion disabled, the wind component along a straight flight
# path is unobservable. Each aircraft's wind estimate can drift differently.
# Both aircraft held IAS 20.00 while ground speeds were 19.3 and 22.05 m/s.
# AHRS_WIND_MAX applies constrain(|V-W|, gnd-MAX, gnd+MAX).
# As an AP_Int8, its smallest effective value is 1. Zero disables clamping.
# The target also uses 1 to keep this setting symmetric.
AHRS_WIND_MAX 1

# Explicitly retain the no-sensor configuration used above.
ARSPD_TYPE 0

# Parameters deliberately inherited from gazebo-plane.parm or defaults:
# AIRSPEED_CRUISE: ArduPlane 4.7 defaults to 12 m/s. The old TRIM_ARSPD_CM
# value 2200 is rejected by this build. The target explicitly uses 20 m/s,
# while the hunter retains the reference default for the A/B comparison.
# formation.py --bumblebee-speed and command_sender.py command flight speed.
# AIRSPEED_MIN/MAX: default envelope 9-22 m/s. The static formation.py
# hunter envelope 15-24 m/s is wider. command_sender.py reads and enforces
# live limits. Keep these A/B tests at or below 22 m/s.
# SERVO*_FUNCTION: the Erenimbus plugin uses elevon, rudder and rotor
# channels. Bumblebee's V-tail and twin-motor mapping, 73/74/79/80/26,
# would route these controls incorrectly on this model.
